00:06:18.432 --> 00:06:20.585
I'm very aggressive.

00:06:20.585 --> 00:06:24.288
And I very aggressively go
after a person and say look as

00:06:24.288 --> 00:06:26.797
quickly as possible I
want you to trust me.

00:06:26.797 --> 00:06:27.977
Tell me what you want.

00:06:27.977 --> 00:06:29.492
What is in your vested interest?

00:06:29.492 --> 00:06:32.464
If I can figure out what that
person wants and first I go with

00:06:32.464 --> 00:06:34.605
honesty and you know it's funny
and when somebody is negotiating

00:06:34.605 --> 00:06:36.739
with you they don't
want to give you honesty.

00:06:36.739 --> 00:06:39.457
And actually I use it as a
tactic to build a relationship.

00:06:39.457 --> 00:06:44.248
If I go at somebody and say look
you guys know this with,

00:06:44.248 --> 00:06:46.036
some of you know 
this with salaries.

00:06:46.036 --> 00:06:48.114
It's how I negotiate 
almost everything.

00:06:48.114 --> 00:06:49.605
I just want to know.

00:06:49.605 --> 00:06:52.833
Because by the way, if you say 
"Hey, I want to pay VaynerMedia

00:06:52.833 --> 00:06:55.430
"four dollars a month," and I want 
four dollars a month well then

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.327
we just saved a lot of time.

00:06:57.327 --> 00:06:59.375
I'm like cool.
Let's do it.

00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:03.202
I think my best tactic has 
been the same which is

00:07:03.202 --> 00:07:06.432
honesty, truth and aggressiveness

00:07:06.432 --> 00:07:09.172
to extract the truth 
from the other person.

00:07:09.172 --> 00:07:11.372
I'm naturally a counter puncher.

00:07:11.372 --> 00:07:13.758
In my marketing and
definitely in my negotiating.

00:07:13.758 --> 00:07:16.453
What do you want to
happen for how much?

00:07:16.453 --> 00:07:19.350
And if I can get them
into a truthful place.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:22.157
Now one of the keys to my
strategy is drawing

00:07:22.157 --> 00:07:23.267
a line in the sand.

00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:26.352
When I say to somebody 
give me your best offer and

00:07:26.352 --> 00:07:27.903
if I can hit, I'll do it.

00:07:27.903 --> 00:07:31.110
If they then give me an 
offer that I can't do

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:33.993
I have to say no 
and I can't move.

00:07:33.993 --> 00:07:36.689
It's all grounded in truths.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:39.399
I think you have to know what
you want and I think you have to

00:07:39.399 --> 00:07:42.393
try to extract from the
other person what they want.

00:07:42.393 --> 00:07:44.598
And you need to try to make 
them feel comfortable that

00:07:44.598 --> 00:07:45.901
you're in their best interest.

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:47.919
One thing I do is I point to
my career at this point and let

00:07:47.919 --> 00:07:50.026
them know I've done everything
on lifetime value that I don't

00:07:50.026 --> 00:07:53.365
need to make much money up
front it's all of the long-term.

00:07:53.365 --> 00:07:54.877
I require that for my people.

00:07:54.877 --> 00:07:56.429
I require that for my partners.

00:07:56.429 --> 00:07:59.830
I just think the right way to
go there is go right at it.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.164
What's going to
get this deal done?

00:08:02.164 --> 00:08:05.248
For me, I'd rather leave profit 
on the table to get the

00:08:05.248 --> 00:08:06.692
deal done quicker.

00:08:06.692 --> 00:08:09.117
I think too many want to
guess the higher number.

00:08:09.117 --> 00:08:12.083
Let that one $8000 for this.

00:08:12.083 --> 00:08:15.165
I think too many people are like
12,000 instead of saying how

00:08:15.165 --> 00:08:19.286
much is it going to get done and
Staphon says 7500 if I'm okay

00:08:19.286 --> 00:08:22.204
with that because I want 8000
I'm like good, done, let's go.

00:08:22.204 --> 00:08:26.719
Speed, movement, trust,
relationships finding a place

00:08:26.719 --> 00:08:28.980
where you can trust that
person you're on the same page.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.845
That's how I see it.

